# Placement

Full contract: `docs/architecture/placement.md`. Hull identity and the
`ComputePlacement` failure taxonomy: `docs/architecture/container_geometry.md`.

## Must

- Enumerate discrete support-surface poses (grid window and/or exact support
  centers). Do not Monte Carlo-sample placement poses from a prior.
- Rest each candidate on `peak = max(height under footprint)` at
  `z = peak + box_height / 2`. Check the complete oriented payload box.
- Allow stacking on previously placed cargo only when the footprint support is
  known. Unobserved columns may land on the a-priori floor
  (`peak ≈ floor_z`, `floor_prior`). Stacking on an unobserved surface is
  `unknown_above_floor`.
- Treat face contact with a placed AABB as support. Positive-volume overlap is
  a capacity reject.
- Prefer low placements when ranking the live Humble solver (`compactness` and
  remaining top clearance). Do not treat a committed box top as a reason to
  stack while a feasible floor slot remains.
- Fill `surface_2d` from live depth and/or a verified measured commit. An
  unverified planned slot, catalog size, or `GetCurrentBox` is not occupancy.
  See `docs/architecture/real_scenario.md` (`RS-1` .. `RS-3`).
- Do not copy `request.placed` from the same unverified plan used to fill
  the height map in order to hide commit–reality disagreement.
- Use the floor prior only as empty-floor existence when no accepted cargo
  map exists. A rejected map must fail closed, not answer from the floor
  prior. Do not treat floor prior as “no cargo inside.”
- Do not require a fake `height_valid=true` box when detection is honestly
  TOP_ONLY (`RS-8`).
- Do not treat `FreeSpaceModel` / `placement_scoring` / the reachability atlas
  as the live Humble `placement_planner_node` path unless that node and
  `docs/architecture/placement.md` switch together.
- Plan place motion (cartesian, OMPL, or later search) against the current
  cargo occupancy at `geometry_hash` / `map_revision`. Occupied and
  unknown-above-floor cells are obstacles for the swept payload and arm.
  URDF plus `scene_manager` boxes are not occupancy (`RS-27`).
- Generate a set of candidate paths when the first is in collision, below
  the cartesian fraction gate, or has no IK. Select among collision-free
  paths by cost with dimension, safety, and efficiency terms. An empty set
  is a motion/path fail-closed reason, not `BIN_FULL`.
